# Node simulator (fake windows)
#
# Every sim drives the tiler against windows that do not exist, asserting on the geometry it
# writes. They need no session, no compositor and no display.
#
# The whole suite, plus the QML passes and the lints:
#   tools/test.sh
#
# One sim while working on it, from the repository root:
#   node src/comp/tests/sim13.mjs src/comp/script/contents/code/kosmic-tiling.mjs keybindings.json
#
# Each sim takes the tiler's path as its first argument, and the ones that check the keymap take
# keybindings.json as the second. A sim that touches the layout core resolves core.mjs as a
# sibling of the tiler it is handed, so point it at the file in its own directory rather than at a
# copy extracted on its own.
#
# tools/test.sh globs this directory, so a new sim is picked up by being written -- locally. CI
# only ever sees what is committed, so an untracked sim passes here and does not exist there, and
# the run is green either way. `git add` it before believing the result.
#
# A new sim has to fail against the behaviour it is pinning down. One that passes whatever the
# tiler does proves nothing, and the way to be sure is to break the branch on purpose and watch
# the assertion fire before trusting it.
